    "settings.mcp.agentSetup.pairPrompt" : {
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "# Pair Starcat CLI\n\n## Goal\n\nThe current AI Agent uses the complete single-use pairing command generated by Starcat, then waits for the user to approve the device in Starcat.\n\n## Single-Use Pairing Command\n\n```bash\n%1$@\n```\n\n## Steps\n\n1. Confirm that the content above is one complete `starcat pair ...` command.\n2. Execute the complete command exactly as provided. Do not edit or split its URI or arguments.\n3. If the CLI starts waiting for approval, instruct the user to return to Starcat.\n4. The user reviews the device information and approves pairing in Starcat.\n5. After pairing succeeds, run:\n\n   ```bash\n   starcat doctor\n   ```\n\n6. If the current macOS/Linux shell cannot find `starcat`, use:\n\n   ```bash\n   \"$HOME/.local/bin/starcat\" doctor\n   ```\n\n## Error Handling\n\n### Expired command\n\nInstruct the user to generate and copy a new pairing prompt from **Starcat > Settings > MCP**.\n\n### Already-used command\n\nInstruct the user to generate a new single-use pairing command. Do not retry an already-used command.\n\n### Pairing rejected by the user\n\nStop and report that the device did not receive Starcat access.\n\n### Starcat is not running\n\nInstruct the user to launch Starcat and enable MCP Service, then run diagnostics again.\n\n## Security Boundaries\n\n- Do not parse, edit, or split the pairing URI.\n- Do not repeat the complete pairing command in the final response.\n- Do not store the pairing command in a repository, configuration file, note, or persistent log.\n- Do not reuse a completed or expired pairing command.\n- Do not request a Local API Key.\n- Do not manually downgrade an HTTPS endpoint to HTTP.\n- Do not run other Starcat commands before pairing completes.\n\n## Final Report\n\nThe current AI Agent reports:\n\n- Whether the CLI accepted the pairing command\n- Whether it entered the Starcat approval stage\n- Whether the user approved the device\n- Whether `starcat doctor` is healthy\n- CLI version, App version, and available tool count\n\nThe final report must not contain the complete pairing command, pairing URI, secret, or other credentials."
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "# 配对 Starcat CLI\n\n## 任务目标\n\n当前 AI Agent 使用 Starcat 生成的完整一次性配对命令连接 CLI，并等待用户在 Starcat 中确认设备。\n\n## 一次性配对命令\n\n```bash\n%1$@\n```\n\n## 执行步骤\n\n1. 确认上方内容是一条完整的 `starcat pair ...` 命令。\n2. 原样执行完整命令，不修改、不拆分其中的 URI 或参数。\n3. 如果 CLI 进入等待确认状态，提示用户返回 Starcat。\n4. 用户在 Starcat 中核对设备信息并确认配对。\n5. 配对成功后运行：\n\n   ```bash\n   starcat doctor\n   ```\n\n6. 如果当前 macOS/Linux shell 找不到 `starcat`，改用：\n\n   ```bash\n   \"$HOME/.local/bin/starcat\" doctor\n   ```\n\n## 异常处理\n\n### 配对命令已过期\n\n提示用户在 Starcat 的「设置 → MCP」中重新生成并复制新的配对提示词。\n\n### 配对命令已使用\n\n提示用户重新生成一次性配对命令。不要重复执行已经使用过的命令。\n\n### 用户拒绝配对\n\n停止后续操作，并报告设备未获得 Starcat 访问权限。\n\n### Starcat 未运行\n\n提示用户启动 Starcat，并确认 MCP Service 已开启，然后重新执行诊断。\n\n## 安全限制\n\n- 不解析、修改或拆分配对 URI。\n- 不在最终回复中复述完整配对命令。\n- 不把配对命令写入仓库、配置文件、笔记或长期日志。\n- 不重复使用已经完成或失效的配对命令。\n- 不向用户索取 Local API Key。\n- 不把 HTTPS endpoint 手工降级为 HTTP。\n- 配对完成前不执行其他 Starcat 命令。\n\n## 完成后报告\n\n当前 AI Agent 最终报告：\n\n- 配对命令是否被 CLI 接受\n- 是否进入 Starcat 确认阶段\n- 用户是否完成确认\n- `starcat doctor` 是否健康\n- CLI 版本、App 版本和可用工具数量\n\n最终报告不得包含完整配对命令、pairing URI、secret 或其他凭据。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
